  "body": "Stacked on #1622 (branch `issue/1607-stock-source-law`; the `keep_law::parts_in_stock` / `neighbour_parts` code exists only there). Fork synced at v0.19.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nSince #1603 / #1607 / #1621 an operation is judged against parts BESIDE its source, but those parts are not in its stamp. A part moved into the cut, added, or un-tagged as a fixture after a clean generation left the op `Ok`. On a turned stock (the program sim refuses to judge) the post read the cached clean verdict and posted into the part.\n\n**Decision: option (c), no stamp term** (`docs/decisions/1628-kept-parts-live-judge.md`). When the program sim cannot judge, the post gate (`posting_sim`, not-judged arm) judges the parts again live:\n- `operation::kept_rejudge::moved_part_problem` runs on each program op whose cached verdict is clean and whose kept part set is non-empty. It collects the op's job again and re-runs, on the cached path, the laws generation ran: the solid law (`contain_into`, `DepthLaw::Keep`), or the budgeted mark law for a stock-source Engrave/Trace. It uses the same cutter, stock to leave, excess and 3+2 frame, and the tap's core acquittal. It checks one kept part at a time, as each part stands now.\n- A cut is refused by name: `stock sim did not judge this program: ... - and N1 now cuts part 'other' (move 328 cuts past the finish surface) - a part moved, added or no longer workholding since it was generated; regenerate it`.\n- An op whose cached warnings already block is skipped, so it is still refused by its own findings, by name.\n- On an aligned stock nothing changes: the sim already judges every part live.\n- `generate::stock_to_leave_of`: the stock-to-leave table is moved out of `run_job_arms` unchanged, so both judges read one number. `contain_into` is now `pub(super)`. `keep_law::kept_parts_named` gives the kept set one mesh per model, by name.\n\nWhy not (a), the stamp term: it breaks the contracts the issue lists. With (c) they all pass unchanged on this branch: `fixtures::workholding_never_stales_a_fresh_toolpath`, `operations::a_frommodel_stock_survives_its_source_being_deleted`, `operations::a_model_update_does_not_touch_a_box_stock`, `fidelity_copies` (both tests), and `stock_source_verdict`. All of these were in the quick gate.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/kept_parts_live.rs`, all on a turned stock)\n- `a_neighbour_moved_into_a_part_source_cut_on_a_turned_stock_is_refused_by_name`: a Trace on B is generated clean, then A is moved into its flank. The op stays Ok, and the post is refused naming `N1` and `other`. With A moved away again, the program posts.\n- `a_part_added_into_a_stock_source_cut_on_a_turned_stock_is_refused_by_name`: a stock-source Slot in the pocket is generated clean, then a boss is added under it. The op stays Ok, and the post is refused naming `S1` and `boss`.\n- `a_fixture_untagged_then_moved_into_a_part_source_cut_on_a_turned_stock_is_refused_by_name`: the clamp is tagged, then untagged. The op stays Ok (the M2.3 law) and the program posts. The clamp is then moved into the cut and the post is refused naming `clamp`.\n- `a_part_moved_into_a_stock_source_cut_on_a_turned_stock_never_posts`: moving the part under a stock-source op already stales it (another stamp input), so the post is refused with \"regenerate\".\n\n## Mutation checks (each line reverted, the test run red, then restored and touched)\n1. The gate's `.or_else(|| kept_moved(..))` replaced with nothing: the 3 `kept_parts_live` refusal tests go red.\n2. The refusal in `moved_part_problem` (`if let Some(w) = ... find(blocks_post)`) never taken: the same 3 go red.\n3. The convicted-op skip in `kept_moved` deleted: red in `stock_source_law` (`engrave_and_trace_off_the_stock_...`, `the_typed_kinds_and_face_...`) and in `neighbour_law::a_cut_on_b_into_its_neighbour_...`. Without the skip, the by-name gouge refusal is displaced.\n4. `marks` forced false (the mark law not used for a stock-source mark): red in `stock_source_law::a_legal_stock_source_cut_stays_clean_and_posts_on_both_stocks`. The re-judge would refuse a legal mark.\n\n## Gate\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/1607-stock-source-law` on 329db7d8: green (app suites 1227 s, ui suites 152 s, 0 failed). Clippy on `camcraft-app` (`--lib --tests -D warnings`) is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- 3+2 (tilted) ops: the cached world path is judged in the frame's local coordinates, as chords at the arc-fit tolerance. No suite has a clean tilted 2D op beside another part, so this arm is not covered by a test.\n- The fail-closed arm for \"the job cannot be collected again\" is unreachable by any fixture: every input `collect_job` can fail on is a stamp input, so such an op reads Stale first.\n- Un-marking raw-stock-only after generation goes through the same live set (`stock_source::judged`). It has no dedicated pin here.\n\nChangelog: A part moved into, added to, or un-tagged inside an operation's cut after generation no longer posts on a turned stock: the post judges the parts beside each op's source again and refuses by name (#1628)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1628\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
